# Binaries
/barkpark
# bin/ holds the committed launcher scripts (Wave 5 personal-local packaging),
# so we do NOT ignore the directory wholesale. Git can't re-include a file once
# its parent dir is excluded, so instead we ignore everything inside bin/ and
# then negate the two scripts we track. Compiled binaries dropped into bin/
# (e.g. by `air`) stay ignored by the wildcard.
bin/*
!bin/barkpark
!bin/barkpark-pg
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Erlang crash dumps (left by a failed BEAM boot)
erl_crash.dump

# Go
vendor/

# bp CLI release binaries (cross-compile artifacts — `make cli-release`)
dist/

# Air (hot reload)
tmp/

# Data
data.json

# Secrets
.env
# Local dev secrets (committed: deploy/*.env.example only)
deploy/*.env
!deploy/*.env.example

# Phoenix API (Elixir)
api/_build/
# Aside/slot build roots (post-merge hook's _build_next, blue/green _build_blue|green)
api/_build_*/
api/deps/
# ...and the same path as a NON-directory. A trailing slash matches directories
# ONLY, so neither this nor api/.gitignore's `/deps/` catches a SYMLINK named
# api/deps — and PR #2907 committed exactly that (mode 120000, target
# /opt/barkpark/api/deps, self-referential on the prod box and DANGLING
# anywhere else, where it stops `mix` from running at all). It only ever
# failed to reach main because a local, uncommitted .git/info/exclude line
# happened to carry the slashless form. A fresh clone has no such guard.
api/deps
# deploy-rebuild.sh's repo-local build mutex (never /tmp — squattable)
.deploy-build.lock
# deploy-rebuild.sh's machine-readable apply record (flight recorder — survives
# the restart-line cgroup kill so a post-restart death is visible)
.deploy-status.json
.deploy-status.json.tmp

# JS monorepo
node_modules/
packages/**/dist/
.artifacts/visual/**/node_modules/
*.log

# doc-truth P5 remake gate — transient reject log (kept out of git).
# Already covered by *.log above; named explicitly so its purpose is
# documented and an editor never re-adds it.
tooling/doc-truth/remake-failures.log

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.worktrees/

# Dolt / DB artifacts
.dolt/
*.db

# Working artifacts — never commit (swept in accidentally by docs-refactor merge, removed 2026-06-10)
.artifacts/
api/.artifacts/
.fidelity-captures/
.visual-runtime/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
api/.claude/

# Scaffy run receipts (bp scaffy run, D35) — machine-local fat records under
# .scaffy/receipts/ that remove-replay inverts; never committed.
.scaffy/

# Host-side deploy state (written by deploy/instance-deploy.sh on the server)
.instance-deploy-last
.slots/
# Site-deploy run-state (DeployRunner's per-run manifests/status/log + transient
# 0600 build-env files, under the repo root so init/1 re-attaches across a restart)
.bp-site-deploy-runs/

# doc-truth generated artifacts (byproducts of the standing --code / --emit-refs runs)
tooling/doc-truth/citation-truth-report.json
tooling/doc-truth/doc-refs.json

# pdrender→TUI wasm — NOT committed (Go js/wasm is not byte-reproducible across
# toolchains). Built at dev (`make dev`), at deploy (scripts/deploy-rebuild.sh),
# and in CI (.github/workflows/pdrender-wasm.yml). The bp-wasm-exec.js loader IS
# committed (host-stable text) and stays tracked.
api/priv/static/assets/bp-pdrender.wasm.gz

# Claude Code harness RUNTIME state — machine-local, never cloned. These lived
# only in one Mac's .git/info/exclude (which git never clones), so a fresh clone
# showed them as untracked noise and could commit another machine's worktrees,
# mailbox, or agent registry. Tracked here so every clone ignores them.
# NOT ignored, deliberately: .claude/workflows/ and .claude/settings.json —
# those ARE the distributed harness and must travel with the repo.
# (.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock is already ignored above — not repeated.)
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
**/.claude/routines/.state/
**/.claude/worktrees/
**/.claude/checkpoints/
**/.claude/mailbox/
**/.claude/agent-registry.json
**/.claude/agent-memory-local
**/.claude/first-run
**/.claude/assistant-daemon-state.json

# lineref-sweep --selftest writes a throwaway probe at the repo root and removes
# it in a finally block; this covers a run killed between the write and the cleanup.
__lineref_selftest_probe_*.ex
